.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-START-TOPIC 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-start-topic \- start delivering a topic's messages, and hand over what it held
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens start-topic
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a stopped topic delivering to its subscribers again, and hands
over everything it held while it was stopped.
.PP
The backlog goes out oldest first \- the order it was published in \-
each message with the body, attributes and priority it was published
with, to the subscriptions the topic has now. A message held at
.I HIGH
priority still arrives at the queue as
.IR HIGH .
The answer says how many were released, and the count is added to the
topic's
.I resend
total.
.SH WHAT A SUBSCRIBER SEES
Exactly what it would have seen at the time, later. There is no marker
saying a message was delayed, no reordering, and no de-duplication: a
subscriber added while the topic was stopped receives the whole backlog,
because the fan-out happens now and it is subscribed now.
.PP
A topic that is already delivering releases nothing and is left as it
is, so running this twice is harmless \- as is running it against a
topic that was never stopped.
.SH INTERRUPTIONS
The backlog is read and delivered a page at a time, and each message is
marked as it goes. A start that is interrupted halfway through has
delivered a prefix of the backlog rather than none of it, and running it
again picks up where it stopped rather than sending the whole thing
twice.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Topic name. A full ERN also works, and is what reaches another
namespace. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The topic is delivering; its ERN, delivery state and the number of
messages released are printed.
.TP
.B 1
No topic of that name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli ens start-topic --topic orders
{"ern":"ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000::topic:orders",
 "status":"RUNNING","released":3}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-stop-topic (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-set-topic-retention (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-messages (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-publish-message (1)
